(4333228, 622641, 29906, '<td valign="top">I think it''s really sad that a large number of voters are automatically scoring down shots simply because of nudity. This particular shot isn''t outstanding in my opinion but it is not horrible either and it definitely does not deserve the 1s, 2s and 3s.<br/> <br/>I think that if someone is offended by nudity that much, then it may be better if don''t vote on it in the first place (similar to how people who are against guns should not be jurors in related cases for example).</td>', 'I think it''s really sad that a large number of voters are automatically scoring down shots simply because of nudity. This particular shot isn''t outstanding in my opinion but it is not horrible either and it definitely does not deserve the 1s, 2s and 3s. I think that if someone is offended by nudity that much, then it may be better if don''t vote on it in the first place (similar to how people who are against guns should not be jurors in related cases for example).', '2007-12-24 14:38:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4333231, 622641, 5885, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> well i kinda thought the same as a lot of people when i first saw it, but i dont think its so far out of the realm of the challenge, i figured this was how she was going to show her husband she spent a chunk of his money and then he wouldn''t be able to get as mad ;) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I didn''t realize it had to follow eBay ToS. The blue ribbon shot certainly doesn''t look like a shot that would be on eBay.<br/> <br/>I just dunno... my eyes are drawn to the necklace, perhaps I''m just calloused to nudity?  I think those that can''t get over the breast, are childish, period.<br/> <br/>I guess I should have just placed the necklace on a plain white background, flat-lit it and scored better.  <br/> <br/>Anyway, it doesn''t matter, because I''m not going to bend over and take DPC-style. I''ll take the ones, but I will create what I like and what I am good at. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-12-24 15:22:47.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: well i kinda thought the same as a lot of people when i first saw it, but i dont think its so far out of the realm of the challenge, i figured this was how she was going to show her husband she spent a chunk of his money and then he wouldn''t be able to get as mad ;)   I didn''t realize it had to follow eBay ToS. The blue ribbon shot certainly doesn''t look like a shot that would be on eBay. I just dunno... my eyes are drawn to the necklace, perhaps I''m just calloused to nudity?  I think those that can''t get over the breast, are childish, period. I guess I should have just placed the necklace on a plain white background, flat-lit it and scored better.   Anyway, it doesn''t matter, because I''m not going to bend over and take DPC-style. I''ll take the ones, but I will create what I like and what I am good at. ', '2007-12-24 14:41:09.000000', '2007-12-24 15:22:47.000000', 0),
