(4338038, 622641, 72318, '<td valign="top">The potato shot was completely different... and if you read my message right then you would realise that the ToS comment was covering the fact that some of the challenge shots are basically "product" shots which fit in with eBay (mine included) - remember - you bought it on Ebay so the product type shot should be one you would expect to find on eBay.  So i was saying that this can''t be one of those so it has to be a "natural environment" shot (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=623012" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">like this</a>,<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=623079" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">or this)</a> or (like the potato one) a "reaction to purchase" shot... This isnt any of the above, and so i was trying to help you understand why i gave this a sub-par score of 4... not to mention the technical problem i put up.<br/> <br/>Dont be bitter about it all, i was only trying to help...</td>', 'The potato shot was completely different... and if you read my message right then you would realise that the ToS comment was covering the fact that some of the challenge shots are basically "product" shots which fit in with eBay (mine included) - remember - you bought it on Ebay so the product type shot should be one you would expect to find on eBay.  So i was saying that this can''t be one of those so it has to be a "natural environment" shot (like this,or this) or (like the potato one) a "reaction to purchase" shot... This isnt any of the above, and so i was trying to help you understand why i gave this a sub-par score of 4... not to mention the technical problem i put up. Dont be bitter about it all, i was only trying to help...', '2007-12-27 07:48:37.000000', NULL, 0),
